[77.746304, "o", "    return lines[0] if lines else \"\""]
[77.746317, "o", "\r\n"]
[77.746343, "o", "\r\n"]
[77.746356, "o", "\r\n"]
[77.746371, "o", "def _step_block_for(plan: str, artifact: dict) -> str:"]
[77.746383, "o", "\r\n"]
[77.746401, "o", "    \"\"\"Return the remediation STEP block that references this artifact (by path, basename, or a"]
[77.746428, "o", "\r\n    match needle); empty string if none.\r\n\r\n    Blocks whose heading marks them as a non-step section — the reconciled change ticket (which"]
[77.746456, "o", "\r\n    Delta-2 requires the agent to reproduce, and which legitimately names every artifact path\r\n    near the top of the plan), an executive summary, an overview — are skipped so they cannot\r\n    shadow the real remediation step below them. Among the remaining step blocks, one that\r\n    carries a verification action is preferred (so a plan that verifies fixes in a dedicated\r\n    validation phase is credited), then the most specific by locator-hit count.\"\"\"\r\n    needles = _needles(artifact)\r\n    matches = [b for b in _coarse_blocks(plan) if any(n in b for n in needles)]\r\n    if not matches:"]
[77.746598, "o", "\r\n        return \"\"\r\n    steps = [b for b in matches if not _NONSTEP_HEADING.search(_block_heading(b))]\r\n    pool = steps or matches  # if the ONLY mention is in a non-step section, fall back to it\r\n    # A plan may verify a fix in-step or in a dedicated validation phase; credit either by\r\n    # preferring, among the artifact's step blocks, one that carries a verification action.\r\n    # Then take the most-specific (most locator hits); ties resolve to document order.\r\n    verified = [b for b in pool if any(v in b.lower() for v in VERIFY_TOKENS)]\r\n    pool = verified or pool\r\n"]
[77.746668, "o", "    return max(pool, key=lambda b: sum(1 for n in needles if n in b))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _phase_of(text: str) -> str:\r\n    \"\"\"Best-guess remediation phase for a block of plan text, by keyword cue.\"\"\"\r\n    low = text.lower()\r\n    # Explicit headers like \"P0 — Contain\" win.\r\n    for phase, cues in PHASE_CUES.items():\r\n        if re.search(rf\"\\b{phase}\\b\", low):\r\n            return phase\r\n    best, best_hits = None, 0\r\n    for phase, cues in PHASE_CUES.items():\r\n        hits = sum(1 for c in cues if c in low)\r\n        if hits > best_hits:\r\n            best, best_hits = phase, hits\r\n    return best or \"eradicate\"\r\n\r\n\r\n_HEADER_RE = re.compile(r\"^\\s*#{1,6}\\s\")\r\n_STEP_RE = re.compile(r\"^\\s*\\d+[.)]\\s\")\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _header_phase(text: str) -> str | None:\r\n    low = text.lower()\r\n    for phase in (\"contain\", \"eradicate\", \"harden\", \"rotate\", \"verify\"):\r\n        if phase in low:\r\n            return phase\r\n    return None\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _ordered_steps(plan: str) -> list:\r\n    \"\"\"Phase label per top-level remediation step, in document order (doc 02 §3.4).\r\n\r\n    Prefers the phase of the enclosing header (\"## P1 — Eradicate\"); sub-bullets such as\r\n    \"- Verify: ...\" are NOT steps and must not be phase-labelled (that spuriously injected a\r\n    'verify' step into every section). Falls back to per-step keyword classification when the\r\n    plan has no phase headers.\"\"\"\r\n    phases, current = [], None\r\n    for line in plan.splitlines():\r\n        if _HEADER_RE.match(line):\r\n            p = _header_phase(line)\r\n            if p:\r\n                current = p\r\n            continue\r\n        if _STEP_RE.match(line):\r\n"]
[77.746682, "o", "            phases.append(current or _phase_of(line))\r\n    if not phases:  # unstructured plan — fall back to block classification\r\n        return [_phase_of(b) for b in _blocks(plan) if b.strip()]\r\n    return phases\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _count_precedence_violations(steps: list, precedence: list) -> int:\r\n    \"\"\"Count adjacent out-of-order transitions against the precedence order.\"\"\"\r\n    idx = [precedence.index(p) for p in steps if p in precedence]\r\n    return sum(1 for a, b in zip(idx, idx[1:]) if a > b)\r\n"]
[77.747394, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@2c3cc1894a47:/app/task# "]
[90.10741, "i", "cat /app/task/solution/solve.sh\n"]
[90.10808, "o", "cat /app/task/solution/solve.sh"]
[90.108153, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[90.108748, "o", "#!/usr/bin/env bash"]
[90.108806, "o", "\r\n"]
[90.108952, "o", "# solution/solve.sh (generated) — Oracle: renders the manifest-derived reports.\r\nset -euo pipefail\r\nOUT=\"${OUTPUT_PATH:-/app}\"\r\nmkdir -p \"$OUT\"\r\ncat > \"$OUT/progress.md\" <<'RK_ORACLE_EOF'"]
[90.108995, "o", "\r\n# Progress\r\n\r\nInvestigation timeline for `ssh-miner`:\r\n\r\n1. Reviewed alerts in `/sas` and enumerated the read-only image at `/disk`.\r\n2. Reconstructed the attack chain: step 1 T1110 — SSH brute force as root; step 2 T1021.004 — SSH login (after step 1); step 3 T1059.004 — shell execution (after step 2); step 4 T1496 — cryptomining (after step 3); step 5 T1053.003 — cron persistence (after step 3); step 6 T1546.004 — bashrc persistence (after step 3); step 7 T1543.002 — systemd persistence (after step 3); step 8 T1070.002 — auth log cleared (after step 3).\r\n3. Swept beyond the alerts for silent artifacts (persistence, tool residue, backdoors).\r\n"]
[90.109124, "o", "4. Authored the four reports and the prioritised remediation plan.\r\nRK_ORACLE_EOF\r\ncat > \"$OUT/intrusion-report.md\" <<'RK_ORACLE_EOF'\r\n# Intrusion Report\r\n\r\n## Entry Point\r\nSSH brute force as root (T1110); SSH login (T1021.004); shell execution (T1059.004). Evidence and reconstruction below; the attack chain is given at the end.\r\n\r\n## Intrusion Entities\r\n| Entity | Evidence | ATT&CK |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| miner-process (process, pid) | `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` | T1496 |\r\n| miner-binary (binary, hash) | `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` | T1496 |\r\n| attack-tool-residue (hydra, brute) | `/home/devops/.bash_history` | T1110 |\r\n\r\n"]
[90.109209, "o", "## Persistence Mechanisms\r\n| Mechanism | Evidence | ATT&CK | Alerted |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| sudoers-backdoor (NOPASSWD) | `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` | T1548.003 | **no** |\r\n| cron | `/var/spool/cron/root` | T1053.003 | yes |\r\n| shell-init | `/root/.bashrc` | T1546.004 | **no** |\r\n| systemd | `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` | T1543.002 | yes |\r\n\r\n## Impact\r\nHost confidentiality, integrity, and availability should be considered compromised until the\r\nremediation plan is executed and verified.\r\n\r\n## Attack Chain\r\nT1110 → T1021.004 → T1059.004 → {T1496, T1053.003, T1546.004, T1543.002, T1070.002}\r\n\r\n"]
[90.109358, "o", "- T1110 → T1021.004\r\n- T1021.004 → T1059.004\r\n- T1059.004 → T1496\r\n- T1059.004 → T1053.003\r\n- T1059.004 → T1546.004\r\n- T1059.004 → T1543.002\r\n- T1059.004 → T1070.002\r\nRK_ORACLE_EOF\r\ncat > \"$OUT/vuln-report.md\" <<'RK_ORACLE_EOF'\r\n# Vulnerability Report\r\n\r\nNo CVE-driven entry vector was identified. The vulnerability scan returned an empty finding\r\nset (`/sas/vulns.json`), and disk evidence attributes initial access to weak-credential and\r\nconfiguration weaknesses rather than exploitation of a software vulnerability.\r\n\r\nConfidence: high. Evidence: `/etc/ssh/sshd_config`, `/etc/my.cnf`, empty `/sas/vulns.json`.\r\nRK_ORACLE_EOF"]
[90.109377, "o", "\r\ncat > \"$OUT/baseline-report.md\" <<'RK_ORACLE_EOF'\r\n# Baseline Report\r\n\r\nConfiguration and baseline weaknesses observed on the host:\r\n\r\n| Weakness | Evidence | Capability |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| ssh-baseline (PermitRootLogin) | `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` | BAS-01 |\r\n| mysql-remote-root (bind-address, 0.0.0.0) | `/etc/my.cnf` | BAS-02 |\r\nRK_ORACLE_EOF\r\ncat > \"$OUT/remediation-plan.md\" <<'RK_ORACLE_EOF'\r\n# Remediation Plan\r\n\r\n## P0 — Contain\r\n1. block attacker source IP inbound.\r\n   - Verify: `iptables -L INPUT -n | grep <ip>`\r\n   - Risk: network\r\n\r\n## P1 — Eradicate\r\n2. quarantine miner binary and terminate the process — target: `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`.\r\n   - Verify: `pgrep -f .xorg returns empty`\r\n   - Risk: runtime\r\n3. remove cron entry from /var/spool/cron/root — target: `/var/spool/cron/root`.\r\n   - Verify: `grep -c '<marker>' /var/spool/cron/root == 0`\r\n   - Risk: runtime\r\n4. remove injected line from /root/.bashrc — target: `/root/.bashrc`.\r\n   - Verify: `grep -c '<marker>' /root/.bashrc == 0`\r\n   - Risk: runtime\r\n5. disable and remove system-update-helper.service — target: `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`.\r\n   - Verify: `systemctl is-enabled system-update-helper 2>&1 | grep -qv enabled`\r\n   - Risk: service\r\n6. remove /etc/sudoers.d/devops NOPASSWD grant — target: `/etc/sudoers.d/devops`.\r\n   - Verify: `! grep -q NOPASSWD /etc/sudoers.d/devops`\r\n   - Risk: auth\r\n\r\n## P2 — Harden\r\n7. set PermitRootLogin no, PasswordAuthentication no, MaxAuthTries 3; reload sshd — target: `/etc/ssh/sshd_config`.\r\n   - Verify: `sshd -T | grep -E 'permitrootlogin|passwordauthentication|maxauthtries'`\r\n   - Risk: auth\r\n8. bind MySQL to localhost and revoke the remote root grant — target: `/etc/my.cnf`.\r\n   - Verify: `grep -q '^bind-address' /etc/my.cnf`\r\n   - Risk: service\r\n\r\n## P3 — Rotate\r\n9. rotate root and devops credentials.\r\n   - Verify: `chage -l root shows a recent change date`\r\n   - Risk: auth\r\n\r\n## P4 — Verify\r\n10. confirm sshd hardening took effect.\r\n   - Verify: `sshd -T | grep permitrootlogin`\r\n   - Risk: auth\r\n11. restart affected services and confirm health.\r\n   - Verify: `systemctl is-active <svc> and HTTP 200 on /`\r\n   - Risk: service\r\nRK_ORACLE_EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@2c3cc1894a47:/app/task# "]
